WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.000
Each branch passes its tests.
Their combination can still fail.

00:04.000 --> 00:10.000
One shared check finds a paired failure.
Jobs one and two are blocked; three and four validate.

00:10.000 --> 00:14.000
Agent A changes DEFAULT_TIMEOUT
from thirty to ten.

00:14.000 --> 00:18.000
Agent B adds TIMEOUT_BUDGET at thirty.
Git merges cleanly, but the test expects equality.

00:18.000 --> 00:22.000
The recorded result holds the conflicting pair
and validates the two compatible branches.

00:22.000 --> 00:26.000
The inspect receipt links job one to job two:
a semantic conflict between their changes.

00:26.000 --> 00:32.000
The operator explicitly dismisses jobs one and two
for this demo, retaining three and four for approval.

00:32.000 --> 00:35.500
This demo authorizes its exact plan
using --expected-plan.

00:35.500 --> 00:38.500
Configured checks rerun before the push
by default.

00:38.500 --> 00:40.500
The push to the local Git remote is atomic.

00:40.500 --> 00:43.000
Verification succeeds for both retained branches.

00:43.000 --> 00:50.000
Two compatible branches landed.
Try uvx mergetrain demo: real CLI output with a disposable local Git remote.
